WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:07.200
Hello, this is a video to show how to wrap label&nbsp;
around cylinder shape packaging mockup in Blender&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.563
this is the 3D model , I made before

00:00:09.563 --> 00:00:14.383
in this&nbsp;video, 
I will add a label and wrap on this 3D food can

00:00:14.383 --> 00:00:20.091
now I add a label
I use Add &gt; Mesh and add a plane

00:00:20.091 --> 00:00:22.667
and then we can go to Edit Mode

00:00:22.667 --> 00:00:27.566
I will rotate to 90°

00:00:27.566 --> 00:00:35.029
and I scale it to 2.12

00:00:35.029 --> 00:00:39.679
this is the length same&nbsp;as the circumference of the cylinder

00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:47.351
so and then I will adjust the height a bit about 0.94

00:00:47.351 --> 00:00:51.272
if we want to wrap the label 
we need more meshes

00:00:51.272 --> 00:00:56.473
so we can right click and subdivide 
to add number of cuts

00:00:56.473 --> 00:01:01.352
in&nbsp;the subdivide panel 
we can increase the number of cuts

00:01:01.352 --> 00:01:07.138
I will use 19 in my case and then we can go to&nbsp;object mode

00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:11.411
and then I want to move the label forwards

00:01:11.411 --> 00:01:15.292
and then I will add the graphics on the label

00:01:15.292 --> 00:01:19.259
we&nbsp;need to add the material 
go to material properties

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:21.790
and add a new material

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:26.391
in the base color 
we can&nbsp;choose image texture

00:01:26.391 --> 00:01:29.715
and then we can link the graphics image

00:01:29.715 --> 00:01:35.377
and then we can open it to put&nbsp;the image into the texture

00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:41.256
then we can switch to material preview to preview the graphics

00:01:41.256 --> 00:01:46.071
to&nbsp;wrap the label we can go to modify properties

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:52.780
and add a modifier, we can choose deform and simpledeform

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:56.387
in the simple deform modifier we can choose bend

00:01:56.387 --> 00:01:59.689
and in the axis we can choose Z

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:04.685
for the&nbsp;angle we can adjust this to 360°

00:02:04.685 --> 00:02:11.583
so the label is wrapped around the cylinder shape of 3D can

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:15.860
if we want to&nbsp;set animation 
we can go to the timeline

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.292
and I go to frame 100 and set one key frame

00:02:20.292 --> 00:02:25.096
and go to the&nbsp;first frame and set it to 0

00:02:25.096 --> 00:02:26.890
and set the keyframe

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:32.196
so we got the simple animation for the wrapped label

00:02:32.196 --> 00:02:33.763
I stop it here

00:02:33.763 --> 00:02:39.610
finally if we want to make the mesh smooth 
we can add the subdivision modifier

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.321
I select the food can and go to add modifier

00:02:43.321 --> 00:02:47.300
generate and choose subdivision surface modifier

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.633
we can do&nbsp;the same thing for the label

00:02:49.633 --> 00:02:55.678
and add the modifier &gt; generate &gt; subdivision surface modifier

00:02:55.678 --> 00:03:00.349
and please noted that 
we can have the Round Edge for the back

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:03.955
so we can go to subdivision surface modifier

00:03:03.955 --> 00:03:11.234
and&nbsp;advanced and in the boundary smooth 
we choose Keep Corner

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:16.742
and then go to object and shade smooth

00:03:16.742 --> 00:03:21.622
this is how we can wrap label around cylinder  packaging mockup in Blender

00:03:21.622 --> 00:03:24.337
thank you for watching this&nbsp;video, hope this help

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:28.092
please subscribe this channel more video will be Shared with you

00:03:28.092 --> 00:03:31.680
I'm artist b, see you in the next video, bye-bye

